    "result_text": "All 44 tests pass with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe locality derivation now prefers the postcode. I made two changes:\n\n**`mapper/Locality.java`** \u2014 added a postcode-preferring overload:\n- New `of(String city, String postcode)` looks up the region by postcode range first (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) via a private `regionForPostcode` helper, and only falls back to the existing city-to-region table when the postcode is absent, blank, non-numeric, or in no known range.\n- The original `of(String city)` (pure city-table lookup) is kept, since `ValidatePostcode` legitimately needs to validate a postcode *against its city's* region \u2014 that must stay city-based, otherwise the postcode would always validate against itself.\n\n**`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `locality` mapping now calls `Locality.of(owner.getCity(), owner.getPostcode())`.\n\nThis returns the same region for known cities (e.g. Sydney + 2000 \u2192 NSW), but a VIC-range postcode (3000) on an otherwise-unknown city now correctly yields VIC, disambiguating same-named cities \u2014 exactly what `Cp30Tests` asserts. The existing postcode-validation behaviour (`Cp29Tests`) is unaffected.",
