    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered trace for creating an owner. The pipeline is defined in `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 a single linear `next:` chain, every step under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the whole create commits once (or rolls back entirely on any escalation). Request body binds to `OwnerFieldsDto`.\n\n## Pre-pipeline gate\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` guards the endpoint (403 on denial). Note: `petclinic.security.enable=false` in `application.properties`, so this is inert unless security is turned on.\n- **Bean validation** \u2014 runs on `@Valid @RequestBody` before step 1's body: `firstName`/`lastName` `@NotNull @Size(1..30)` + name `@Pattern`; `address` `@NotNull @Size(1..255)`; `city` `@NotNull @Size(1..80)`; `telephone` `@NotNull @Size(1..20)`; `email` `@Size(max 255)`; `postcode` `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`. Failure \u2192 400 (`MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 `ValidationExceptionHandler`). `email`, `postcode`, `registrationDate`, `sharesHousehold` are optional; `sharesHousehold` is write-only.\n\n## Pipeline steps, in order\n\n**Validations (reject with an error status):**\n1. **ValidateOwnerFields** \u2014 binds/publishes the body; rejects whitespace-only `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`, `address` \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400). *Only step that reads `@RequestBody`.*\n2. **ValidatePostcode** \u2014 if postcode present and city's region known (Sydney/Melbourne/Brisbane), the 4 digits must fall in that state's range \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n3. **NormalizeOwnerTelephone** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 rewrites telephone to E.164 in place; must be 8\u201315 digits and match known country-code lengths (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210) \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400).\n4. **NormalizeOwnerEmail** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 blank \u2192 null; if present must match email regex \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` (400); stored lower-cased.\n5. **NormalizeOwnerAddress** *(side-effect)* \u2014 canonicalizes address (trim, collapse spaces, upper-case, expand ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE).\n6. **CheckOwnerCityCapacity** \u2014 if the city already has \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n7. **CheckOwnerDailyLimit** \u2014 computes effective business day (given `registrationDate` or today, weekend rolled to Monday); if \u2265 100 owners already have that date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (429).\n\n**Side-effects (build up and persist the entity):**\n8. **BuildOwner** \u2014 maps DTO \u2192 `Owner`, sets `registrationDate` to the effective business day; publishes the entity.\n9. **CountNamesakes** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n10. **AssignCustomerCode** \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (per-city sequence, zero-padded).\n11. **AssignMembershipNumber** \u2014 sets `membershipNumber` = `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (registration year).\n12. **AssignHousehold** \u2014 if `sharesHousehold=true` and an existing owner shares normalized last name + address: derives a stable `householdId` and **writes it back onto existing housemates (saves them)** \u2014 a persistence side-effect before the main save.\n13. **CheckOwnerIdentityUnique** *(validation)* \u2014 builds `identityKey = telephone|email|householdId`; duplicate against any existing owner \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n14. **SaveOwner** \u2014 `ownerRepository.save(owner)` (assigns id).\n15. **AuditOwnerCreated** \u2014 logs id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel to the `AUDIT` logger.\n16. **MarkBulkSignupWarning** \u2014 sets transient `bulkSignupWarning=true` if > 80 owners registered on today's business day (response-only, not persisted).\n17. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** \u2014 maps `Owner` \u2192 `OwnerDto`, responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n- The real URL is **`POST /petclinic/api/owners`** \u2014 `server.servlet.context-path=/petclinic/` is set, though the `Location` header hardcodes `/api/owners/{id}` and omits that prefix.\n- Because every step runs under the one transaction, a late failure (e.g. `DuplicateIdentityException` at step 13) rolls back the household back-fill writes from step 12.\n- Escalation handler mapping oddity: `DataIntegrityViolationException` (possible from `SaveOwner`) maps to **404**, not 409/500.\n\nI read via a search agent rather than opening each file myself; if you want, I can quote the exact source of any specific step (e.g. the E.164 or identity-key logic) to confirm a detail."
